  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Warm weather conditions expected to be the \ndominant factor today, with high temperatures several degrees above \nnormal to near 90 degrees. By Saturday, strong, gusty winds are \nanticipated as the surface pressure gradient tightens, with \nsustained wind speeds up to 20-25 mph and gusts near 45 mph. High \ntemperatures will still be a few degrees above normal, but cooler \nair begins to move in, keeping highs in the 80s with much of the \ncold air reaching by midnight as lows drop into the 40s with a few \nvalleys into the 30s. Sunday, winds will be much weaker with a few \nbreezy gusts up to 20 mph in the afternoons. Temperatures shift to \nthe opposite spectrum with highs now expected to be several degrees \nbelow normal this time of year with highs in the 60s-70s (80s for \nparts of central Nevada in N. Nye County and White Pine County).\nOvernight lows drop to near freezing temperatures in the 30s and\n40s with some valleys below freezing. Monday is expected to see\nmuch the same as Sunday with highs several degrees below normal\nand overnight lows in the 30s to 40s. By Tuesday and into mid-\nweek, temperatures will slightly warm up but stay within normal.",
